<h2 id='what-is-cloudways'>☁️ What Is Cloudways?</h2>

<p>Cloudways is a managed cloud hosting platform that sits between you and the major infrastructure providers — DigitalOcean, AWS, Google Cloud, Linode, and Vultr. Instead of provisioning your own server and configuring Nginx, PHP-FPM, Redis, and SSL from scratch, Cloudways handles all of that through a clean dashboard while you retain root-level control when you need it.</p>

<p>For med spa operators, that distinction matters. You're not a DevOps engineer — you're running a clinical business. But you also can't afford the performance ceiling of a $5/month shared host when a slow booking page is costing you consult conversions. Cloudways occupies exactly that middle ground: enterprise-grade infrastructure without requiring a sysadmin on staff.</p>

<p>The platform launched in 2011 and has matured considerably. As of 2026, it supports one-click staging environments, built-in Cloudflare CDN integration, automated backups, and a PHP version manager — all features that matter when you're maintaining a WordPress or custom site for a med spa practice. For a deeper look at how hosting fits into your broader digital stack, see our <a href='https://medspaoperator.io/guides/med-spa-website-essentials'>med spa website essentials guide</a>.</p>

