<h2 id='our-experience'>🧪 Our Experience Testing Cloudways for Aesthetic Clinics</h2>

<p>Our team has evaluated website and booking infrastructure across dozens of aesthetic practices — from solo injector studios to multi-location dermatology groups managing thousands of patient visits per month. We've watched hosting choices directly affect Google Ads Quality Scores, organic rankings, and checkout completion rates on treatment packages.</p>

<p>We ran Cloudways on a DigitalOcean 2GB server ($28/mo at time of testing) hosting a WordPress site built to replicate a typical med spa: service pages, a before/after gallery with 40+ images, a Webflow-embedded booking widget, and a contact form tied to a CRM webhook. We benchmarked against a comparable WP Engine Startup plan and a SiteGround GrowBig account.</p>

<p>Results across a 30-day monitoring window using Uptime Robot and GTmetrix:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Uptime:</strong> 99.97% — one 8-minute degradation event tied to a DigitalOcean NYC3 region incident</li>
  <li><strong>Average TTFB:</strong> 163ms from US-East (vs. 390ms on SiteGround, 210ms on WP Engine)</li>
  <li><strong>GTmetrix Grade:</strong> A (94 Performance, 95 Structure) after enabling Redis object cache</li>
  <li><strong>Time to Interactive on mobile:</strong> 2.1 seconds on a simulated 4G connection</li>
</ul>

<p>Those numbers matter in the real world. A med spa running Google Ads to a landing page with a 2.1s TTI on mobile is going to see meaningfully better conversion rates than one loading in 4+ seconds. <a href='https://medspaoperator.io/guides/google-ads-med-spa'>Our Google Ads guide for med spas</a> breaks down exactly how page speed factors into campaign profitability.</p>

