<h2 id='key-features'>🔑 Key Features for Med Spa Websites</h2>

<h3>Managed WordPress Performance Stack</h3>
<p>Cloudways pre-configures Apache or Nginx with PHP-FPM, Varnish cache, Memcached, and Redis on every server. For med spa WordPress sites running Divi, Elementor, or a custom theme with WooCommerce for product sales, this stack dramatically outperforms default shared hosting configurations. You don't have to touch a config file to get these gains.</p>

<h3>One-Click Staging Environments</h3>
<p>Every application on Cloudways gets a one-click staging clone. For med spa operators updating their site before a major promotion — a new treatment menu, seasonal pricing, or a rebrand — the ability to test changes on a live clone before pushing to production is genuinely valuable. We've seen practices lose a full day of bookings after a botched plugin update on a live site. Staging eliminates that risk.</p>

<h3>Team Collaboration and Access Controls</h3>
<p>If you work with an external marketing agency or web developer, Cloudways lets you grant team access with granular permissions. You can give a developer SSH access without handing over your billing credentials. For multi-provider practices where HIPAA-adjacent data hygiene matters, keeping access scoped is a real operational win.</p>

<h3>Cloudflare Enterprise CDN Integration</h3>
<p>Cloudways bundles Cloudflare's Enterprise CDN tier through its "Cloudways Bot Protection" add-on and its built-in Cloudflare integration. Even on the free integration, your before/after gallery images, CSS, and JS files serve from edge nodes globally. For med spas targeting local SEO in competitive markets like Miami, NYC, or LA — where your patients may be researching from mobile on variable connections — CDN delivery is a direct ranking and conversion factor.</p>

<h3>Automated Backups with Off-Server Storage</h3>
<p>Daily automated backups are included, with retention configurable up to 4 weeks. Backups store off-server, meaning a server failure doesn't take your backup with it. You can also trigger on-demand backups before any significant change. This is the baseline we expect from any host handling a business-critical site.</p>

<h3>PHP Version Management</h3>
<p>Med spa websites frequently run third-party plugins for HIPAA-compliant forms, CRM integrations, and booking embeds. These plugins don't always keep pace with PHP updates. Cloudways lets you switch PHP versions per application from the dashboard in under a minute — no ticket to support, no waiting. We've used this exact feature when a Jotform HIPAA plugin broke on PHP 8.2 and needed a temporary rollback.</p>

