<h2 id='who-its-for'>🎯 Who Cloudways Is (and Isn't) For</h2>

<p><strong>Cloudways is the right call if you are:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>A single or multi-location med spa running WordPress and spending money on paid traffic — your landing page speed directly affects your cost per lead</li>
  <li>Working with a marketing agency or freelance developer who needs scoped server access</li>
  <li>Currently on shared hosting and hitting unexplained slowdowns during high-traffic periods (post-email blast, flash sale announcements, etc.)</li>
  <li>Selling retail products or treatment packages through WooCommerce and need reliable uptime during promotions</li>
  <li>Running a content-heavy site with an active blog targeting local SEO keywords — see our <a href='https://medspaoperator.io/guides/med-spa-seo-strategy'>med spa SEO strategy guide</a> for how hosting speed feeds into organic rankings</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Cloudways probably isn't right if you are:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>A brand-new solo practitioner with zero technical comfort and a $500 total website budget — start with a managed WordPress host like WP Engine Startup or Flywheel until you have volume to justify the upgrade</li>
  <li>Running a simple booking-only site with no blog, no gallery, and minimal traffic — a $20/month shared host with a good CDN will serve you fine</li>
  <li>Needing cPanel-based hosting because your current plugins or workflows are locked to it</li>
</ul>

